distance was related to cognition, but walking speed was not. It seems that even moderate levels of physical activity can serve to limit declines in cognition in older adults. The Power of Music I have often wondered what it is about music that eli and non-autistic children, comparing those with similar cits emotions. Philosophers and biologists have asked the language skills, and asked the kids to match the music to drawn to music. ferent feelings in music did not depend on their diagno- Some scientists conclude that music’s influence may sis. Autistic and typical children with similar verbal skills be a chance event, arising from its ability to hijack brain performed equally well, indicating that music can reliably systems built for other purposes such as language, emo- convey feelings even in people whose ability to pick up tions and movement. As Harvard University psycholo- emotion-laden social cues, such as facial expressions or gist Steven Pinker famously puts it, music is “auditory tone of voice, is severely compromised. cheesecake”, a confection crafted to tickle the areas of the Music’s ability to convey feelings may underlie one of its mind that evolved for more important functions. But as most important benefits. In most cultures, music is always a result of chance, music seems to offer a novel system a communal event: everyone gets together to sing, dance of communication rooted in emotions rather than mea- and play instruments. Even in Western societies, which ning. Recent d', 'a4ecc0ce7c5a', '["Music is understood in much the same way regardless of people’s origins","Music has been viewed as part of religious spiritual healing","Music and mathematics trigger the same emo tions in people","Music brings out unexpected reactions in people according to recent research"]'::jsonb, 'A', '2013ht_provpass-1-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2013ht', 1, 33),
