 of a pricing model criticized as an antiquated old media legacy by detractors, but the reason it is still used in China is because that’s the way most online advertisers, usually small and medium-sized companies with limited resources, like it. Cost-per-day not only has the benefit of familiarity, but with credible data thin on the ground it also provides a relatively reliable way of gauging the reach of digital campaigns. Lost Women of Science In December 1788, the astronomer royal, Dr Nevil Mas- women’s exclusion from learned bodies. She questioned kelyne, Fellow of the Royal Society, wrote to 38-year-old the Baconian notion of relentless mechanical progress Caroline Herschel congratulating her on being “the first in her polemic Observations on Experimental Philosophy woman in the history of the world” to discover not one, (1668). She also produced arguably the first-ever science- but two new comets. Her celebrity would, as the director fiction story, The Blazing World (1666), which considered of the Paris Observatory noted, “shine down through the the alternative futures of science. All this earned her the ages”. sobriquet “Mad Madge”. Dr Maskelyne hoped Caroline Herschel did not feel The first original paper that might be considered as part isolated among the male community of astronomers in of a scientific research programme conducted by a woman Britain and “for the benefit of terrestrial astronomy, will and published in the Royal Society’s journ', '9f5a60f1e469', '["They wrote a large number of books on the history of science.","They made it easy for scientists to reach out to different communities.","They highlighted the threat of science to ordinary citizens.","They discussed science in relation to people’s everyday lives."]'::jsonb, 'D', '2014ht_provpass-1-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2014ht', 1, 34),
('What are we told about Margaret Caven- dish?', 'ELF', 'verbal', 'Today’s Fiction Question Our planet is getting mad as hell and it isn’t going to take 31. What is the main point here? it any longer. It’s an old theme but a rich one, and in the 1950s and 60s it provided plots for dozens of science-fic- A Environmental fiction is now a regular part of tion disaster novels. Cities were drowned, oceans eradica- contemporary literature. ted and pastures killed off as authors subjected civilisation B Science fiction and eco-thrillers are pure to indignities – apocalyptic literature that mirrored the storytelling. era’s cold war uncertainties. Today, this kind of storytelling C Environmental fiction is best described as books has taken on a harder edge and eco-thrillers have become on catastrophes and wars. a more robust genre on the page and the screen. Environ- mental fiction is moving away from its roots in science fiction in its criticism of modern society. fiction and becoming part of mainstream literature – as is revealed by some of the most recent novels to tackle climate change and the like. Online Advertising Question Digital media’s big sale push worldwide may centre on 32. What is suggested about online how easy it is for marketers to measure the performance advertising in China? of online advertising campaigns, but such issues tend to get pushed to the side in China, home to the world’s lar- A It is evaluated in the same way as in the rest of gest internet population. Most online advertising in the the world. Middle Kingdom, much like neighbouring Japan and B Medium-sized businesses cannot afford online Korea, is not priced by how many people have seen an ad, advertising. or how many people were intrigued enough to click on C It is nowadays less frequently used than in Japan. it, but how long an ad is posted on a site. There has been no shortage of forecasting over the years, predicting the online advertising. demise of a pricing model criticized as an antiquated old media legacy by detractors, but the reason it is still used in China is because that’s the way most online advertisers, usually small and medium-sized companies with limited resources, like it. Cost-per-day not only has the benefit of familiarity, but with credible data thin on the ground it also provides a relatively reliable way of gauging the reach of digital campaigns. Lost Women of Science In December 1788, the astronomer royal, Dr Nevil Mas- women’s exclusion from learned bodies. She questioned kelyne, Fellow of the Royal Society, wrote to 38-year-old the Baconian notion of relentless mechanical progress Caroline Herschel congratulating her on being “the first in her polemic Observations on Experimental Philosophy woman in the history of the world” to discover not one, (1668). She also produced arguably the first-ever science- but two new comets. Her celebrity would, as the director fiction story, The Blazing World (1666), which considered of the Paris Observatory noted, “shine down through the the alternative futures of science. All this earned her the ages”. sobriquet “Mad Madge”. Dr Maskelyne hoped Caroline Herschel did not feel The first original paper that might be considered as part isolated among the male community of astronomers in of a scientific research programme conducted by a woman Britain and “for the benefit of terrestrial astronomy, will and published in the Royal Society’s journ', '9f5a60f1e469', '["She was a multifaceted writer who questioned many aspects of science.","She led an immoral life and was therefore not invited to lecture on science.","She distrusted most scientists of her time and wrote about it in her poems.","She was a brilliant scientist who was diagnosed with a mental disorder. AND HERE ARE SOME SHORTER TEXTS: Health Care As the health care reform rolls out over the next five years and millions of newly insured seek treatment, the shor- tage of general-medicine doctors will only worsen. Many researchers anticipate that physician assistants (PAs) and nurse practitioners will step in to fill that gap. They are already on the front lines, handling more and more rou- tine visits, and their numbers are expected to increase in the coming years. Researchers are finding that the presence of PAs and nurse practitioners at doctors’ offices may help improve both the quality and availability of medical care. Fish Our birds may be in trouble, but life is looking up for our fish, according to our leading supermarket chains. They are reporting soaring sales of so-called alternative fish, including pollack, dab, mussels, squid and sardines, in place of once-staple cod, haddock, tuna and farmed sal- mon. The switch in customer preferences was apparently sparked by a television campaign, Fish Fight. It highligh- ted the wastefulness of “discard” fishing practices, which involves throwing back dead and dying fish that are sur- plus to catch quotas, or else unwanted by fishmongers and supermarkets. – 14 Cleopatra More than two millennia after it took place, the story of Cleopatra has lost none of its grip on the world’s imagi- nation. It has inspired great plays, novels, poems, movies, works of art, musical compositions both serious and silly, and of course histories and biographies. Yet, for all this rich documentation and interpretation, it remains at least as much legend and mystery as historical record, which has allowed everyone who tells it to play his or her own variations on the many themes it embraces. – 15"]'::jsonb, 'A', '2014ht_provpass-1-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2014ht', 1, 35),
