mbay in of slavery, the focus was naturally on the shipment of Afri- an Arab ship and who were brought overland in covered can slaves to the West Indies, but no mention was made of carriages. Wajid Ali Shah’s own father ordered 200 swords the trade eastwards from Africa to the Indian subcontinent for his African troops. So the custom of employing Afri- or of the Arab traders who sold slaves to wealthy Indian cans and an overland slave-trading route was already estab- rulers. Although a few Africans rose to positions of power lished. As many as 1,000 male and female African slaves in India, some even establishing small kingdoms, most may have arrived in Lucknow in 1847 and 1848. Although entered the country as slaves. Their descendants are found Africans were employed elsewhere in India, the Nawabs of today in Gujarat and along the southern coast. But little Oudh seem unique in importing women as well as men. is known about those slaves shipped in through Bombay In 1860, with the British firmly back in control, the and Karachi and taken eastwards to be sold. remaining Africans in Lucknow petitioned the Chief Anecdotal stories of African soldiers fighting against Commissioner for pensions. This was not a completely the British during the Indian Mutiny (also known as the futile hope because many people who had been dependent Indian Uprising) occur in military memoirs and par-', '762c63aa2bf7', '["There were more Africans sold as slaves to India than to the West Indies.","Not all Africans in India were imported as slaves.","There are hardly any traces left in India of the Africans who were once slaves.","Most slaves in India were of African origin."]'::jsonb, 'B', '2015ht_provpass-1-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2015ht', 1, 33),
