 Subsequently What else should governments be doing? That they have a role in address- ing the health problems caused by obesity is beyond 35_____, not least 35. because they bear much of the cost of dealing with such problems. In the A reason US, economists estimate the cost of obesity-related healthcare and lost pro- B debate ductivity at between $147 billion and $190 billion a year. Thus, the need to C relevance act is urgent. But how? D belief Marion Nestle, New Scientist Preventive Medicine In 1796, an English country doctor named Edward Jen- As late as the 1950s, parents had been encouraged to expose ner successfully immunized a child against smallpox, the their children to diseases like measles and mumps in order world’s deadliest infectious disease. News of Jenner’s stun- to get them over with before adulthood, when the dangers ning achievement led millions throughout Europe to roll increased. Vaccines for these illnesses have been around up their sleeves. Yet, as Arthur Allen makes clear in Vac- since the 1970s. More were on the way and some research- cine, a timely, fair-minded and crisply written account ers spoke openly about a future without infectious disease. of “medicine’s greatest lifesaver,” not everyone welcomed In our current age of AIDS, one marvels at the arrogance Jenner’s feat. Criticism came quickly, often in apocalyptic of such a belief. Nature remains a full step ahead. terms. The economist Thomas Malthus wrote that vac- Allen is sympathetic to parental fears regarding the dan- cination might lead to dangerous population increases. gers of', '38eed07682e6', '["The success of 20th century vaccination programs has made it less necessary to vaccinate today’s children.","It is doubtful whether the overall, long-term effects of vaccination are positive.","Recent developments will have to be met by serious consideration of the pros. and cons of vaccination.","The discovery of new diseases for which there are no vaccines is unavoidable. PROVET ÄR SLUT. FINNS TID ÖVER, KONTROLLERA DINA SVAR."]'::jsonb, NULL, '2016ht_provpass-4-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2016ht', 4, 40),
