tire D They are a result of people’s unethical drive to edifice of capitalism is based on capital – which is really make more money than they need. just another word for confidence. If people believe your confidence to be authentic, the risk you take is likely to be small. But as soon as people think you are bluffing, they panic – and panic destroys wealth faster than confidence can ever increase it. Verbaldel ELF16A V1.indd 11 2016-01-07 13:27:46 New Orleans When Hurricane Katrina hit New Orleans in late August asters and an almost constant sense of flux. Partly this was 2005, the city and its people suffered wounds that are still a result of its location. Or, as New Orleans Mayor Marc healing. While the rebuilding efforts continue apace, every Morial put it in 2001: ‘This was a lousy place to put a city.’ one seems to agree that the city that eventually emerges Unsurprisingly, therefore, the city’s particular relationship from the wreckage will be very different to the “old” New with catastrophe has long been proverbial. Orleans. But it was not just the physical city that was As bad as hurricanes and conflagrations and potential devastated by Katrina. Equally damaged was its carefully slave rebellions could be, perhaps no single threat was cultivated image as the city that care forgot. Shocked by more pressing and more characteristic of 19th-century the indelible images of destructio', 'd28608502767', '["There is little reason why the city should see itself as a tourist magnet.","It has played down those aspects of its history that do not fit in with its tourist image.","The city has failed to exploit the full commercial potential of modern tourism.","Its promotion of itself as a major tourist attraction is mainly the result of its glorious past."]'::jsonb, 'B', '2016vt_provpass-2-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2016vt', 2, 33),
