aft. The Brothers Grimm We all know the stories of the Brothers Grimm. We’ve Indeed, parents are some of the primary figures of dan- seen them brought to life in films, cartoons and plays, but ger in the Brothers Grimm fairy tales. Interestingly, the true Grimms’ tales are pure folklore, passed down while later versions took steps to (slightly) tone down from generation to generation and, like all the best sto- the horror with wicked stepmothers, the earliest ver- ries, they were spoken. sions feature biological parents taking the most drastic, It was that oral tradition of storytelling that first drew terrifying measures. Take Hansel and Gretel, for example. the brothers to these classics. Jacob and Wilhelm were These days, it’s the woodcutter’s new wife who is largely tremendously proud of their national heritage, and col- responsible for abandoning the children in the woods, lecting fairy tales was an opportunity to preserve and with the husband a reluctant and remorseful accomplice celebrate a popular German tradition. who later comes back for his children. In the earliest ver- The enduring image of the Grimms is of two travel- sion, it is the unlucky siblings’ own mother who propels ling scholars, journeying far and wide across the land to this evil plan, and their father is just as complicit. Simi- track down these stories and record them for posterity. larly, we all think of the wicked queen in Snow White as The truth, of course, is somewhat different.', '79ef3075e56b', '["It was a result of hearing many stories in their own childhood.","They saw stories as a means to protect the culture of the German people.","It was a result of regularly encountering story tellers at local gatherings.","They saw stories as a chance to spread German ideals outside their own country."]'::jsonb, NULL, '2021vta_provpass-1-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2021vta', 1, 33),
