No Child Left Undiagnosed Unless we soon come to our senses, the United States permission to advertise directly to consumers, a practice may become a dystopia of overdiagnosed mental illness, allowed only in the United States and New Zealand. The starting with early childhood. Already, one in five adults results? A sector delivering annual sales close to $10 bil- takes psychotropic medication on a daily basis. One in lion – and thousands of kids taking medicine they prob- four of us has qualified for a psychiatric diagnosis in the ably don’t need. last year, and half of us will have been diagnosed with a Some child psychologists have now proposed a wholly mental disorder at some point in our lifetime. new condition, closely related to ADHD, that could poten- The statistics for children and teenagers are even tially subject millions more children, especially younger more alarming: a recent study found that by age 21, 81 kids, to reckless diagnosis and treatment. “Sluggish cog- percent of American kids could be labeled with a mental nitive tempo” (SCT) may be the most ill-informed inven- disorder – if they are evaluated often enough and with tion I have encountered in my 40 years of evaluating sufficient diagnostic ardor. diagnostic wish lists. In the past 20 years, the rate of attention deficit hyper- To date, SCT’s main characteristics are vaguely activity disorder (ADHD) diagnoses has tripled: 11 per- described and still under discussion, but include', 'c4ed70f4f133', '["The actual situation is even worse than has sometimes been assumed.","Young people tend to suffer from mental ill- being more often than before.","There seems to be no obvious cure in sight for the foreseeable future.","The figures for mental disorder in the U.S. are clearly exaggerated."]'::jsonb, 'D', '2023ht_provpass-3-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2023ht', 3, 33),
