('What is implied here?', 'ELF', 'verbal', 'American Folk Music Question The national treasure that is American folk and country 31. What is said here about the relationship music came over on boats from the British Isles in the between British and American folk songs? 17th century, especially the Scots-Irish borderlands. It traveled down the Appalachian – via fiddle, banjo and were replaced. guitar – in ballads and hymns, the words changing into new songs but the music immutable. For example, it B The original British folk songs developed beyond was the first music that the great American songwriter recognition. Woody Guthrie ever heard: his mother singing Anglo- C American folk music gradually lost touch with its Celtic ballads in a high nasal country twang at their home British roots. outside Okemah, Oklahoma. with new music. The Great Lakes Question The Great Lakes are undergoing “an ecological catas- 32. What is implied here? trophe unlike any this continent has seen,” according to Pulitzer Prize finalist Dan Egan. Humans have dramati- A Measures against environmental destruction tend to be taken when it is already too late. cally altered the lakes’ fauna since invasive species first snuck up through the man-made Saint Lawrence Seaway. B Environmental damage caused by chemical Blunders sometimes stemmed from well-meaning poli- waste is usually very difficult to repair. cies. Researchers imported Asian carp to kill river nui- C The chemical industry is unlikely to take sances without chemicals, and now some worry the fish responsibility for effects on the environment. has silently invaded Lake Michigan’s floor via the Chi- cago Sanitary and Ship Canal. And the lakes’ imported protect the environment can be difficult. problems are quickly becoming national disasters, such as the tiny and quick-spawning quagga mussel that has infested regions as far away as Lake Mead and Lake Pow- ell on the Colorado River. No Child Left Undiagnosed Unless we soon come to our senses, the United States permission to advertise directly to consumers, a practice may become a dystopia of overdiagnosed mental illness, allowed only in the United States and New Zealand. The starting with early childhood. Already, one in five adults results? A sector delivering annual sales close to $10 bil- takes psychotropic medication on a daily basis. One in lion – and thousands of kids taking medicine they prob- four of us has qualified for a psychiatric diagnosis in the ably don’t need. last year, and half of us will have been diagnosed with a Some child psychologists have now proposed a wholly mental disorder at some point in our lifetime. new condition, closely related to ADHD, that could poten- The statistics for children and teenagers are even tially subject millions more children, especially younger more alarming: a recent study found that by age 21, 81 kids, to reckless diagnosis and treatment. “Sluggish cog- percent of American kids could be labeled with a mental nitive tempo” (SCT) may be the most ill-informed inven- disorder – if they are evaluated often enough and with tion I have encountered in my 40 years of evaluating sufficient diagnostic ardor. diagnostic wish lists. In the past 20 years, the rate of attention deficit hyper- To date, SCT’s main characteristics are vaguely activity disorder (ADHD) diagnoses has tripled: 11 per- described and still under discussion, but include', 'c4ed70f4f133', '["Measures against environmental destruction tend to be taken when it is already too late.","Environmental damage caused by chemical waste is usually very difficult to repair.","The chemical industry is unlikely to take responsibility for effects on the environment.","Predicting the consequences of actions to protect the environment can be difficult. permission to advertise directly to consumers, a practice allowed only in the United States and New Zealand. The results? A sector delivering annual sales close to $10 bil- lion – and thousands of kids taking medicine they prob- ably don’t need. Some child psychologists have now proposed a wholly new condition, closely related to ADHD, that could poten- tially subject millions more children, especially younger kids, to reckless diagnosis and treatment. “Sluggish cog- nitive tempo” (SCT) may be the most ill-informed inven- tion I have encountered in my 40 years of evaluating diagnostic wish lists. To date, SCT’s main characteristics are vaguely described and still under discussion, but include some combination of daydreaming, mind wandering, lethargy, and slow mental processing. Although no scientific con- sensus exists, its proponents claim that up to 2 million children may already qualify for the diagnosis, which, improbably, appears to be racing toward clinical recogni- tion. This can only be described as a public health experi- ment seeking to mislabel millions more kids as “patients.” Such shaky diagnostic suggestions typically come from “experts” brimming with confidence. Sometimes they are well-meaning, sincerely seeking to aid strug- gling families. Sometimes they are overly influenced by drug company support of their research. But rarely are they guided by common sense or an appropriate fear of unintended consequences. Unsurprisingly, some of the same experts who succeeded in expanding ADHD diag- nosis are now advancing this new disorder, a potential disaster for the kids who would be misdiagnosed and then overmedicated. It is time for policymakers to restrict drug company influence and for clinicians to realize that an accurate diagnosis requires time and watchful waiting. It is time for parents to step up and protect their kids, to become informed consumers, to get second opinions, and to try other approaches before resorting to medication. Finally, it is time that we improve our school systems rather than medicate our students. Instead of spending billions a year on drugs, how about providing kids with smaller classes and more gym periods so that they can blow off steam more naturally, without prescription? Allen Frances, M.D., Psychology Today"]'::jsonb, 'D', '2023ht_provpass-3-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2023ht', 3, 32),
