ign ing, drawing and inking, but the reward is a work of art which 35. readers treat differently to a book with only a cover plate. Many keep their objects of beauty in plastic envelopes and repeatedly B method return to them, maybe just one page, for it is the visceral qual C artwork ity of the 35 that compels. D language Ian Gordon, New Internationalist Mystery Script Boasting illustrations of naked nymphs, unrecognisa information value of each chunk. In novels or chapters ble plants, astrological diagrams and reams of text in an that pertain to a certain topic, clusters of related, high- unknown alphabet, the Voynich manuscript has baffled entropy terms – known as scale domains – tend to be and captivated researchers since book dealer Wilfred large, containing several hundred words. By contrast, Voynich found it in an Italian monastery in 1912. in a simple list of citations, say, these domains would be Although its patterns of word lengths and symbol com much smaller. binations seem similar to those of real languages, the The team calculated the optimal scale domains for most recent studies suggested that the book is a clever texts of similar length to Voynich, written in several lan 15th-century hoax designed to dupe Renaissance book guages: On the Origin of Species (English), Records of the collectors, and that the words have no meaning. Grand Historian (Classical Chinese) and The Confessions Now Marcelo Montemurro of the Universi', '86513db84b99', '["The copy found in 1912 is unlikely to be the original manuscript.","It is likely that most of the plants depicted in the script have never existed.","The text appears to be more similar to Latin than to English or Chinese.","Studying word occurrence can show whether or not the text is a fake."]'::jsonb, 'D', '2024ht_provpass-5-verbal-hpguiden-se.pdf', '2024ht', 5, 36),
